===Grand Aman===
{{Main|Grand Aman}}

The '''Grand Aman''' (ⴰⵎⴰⵏ ⴰⵎⵇⵔⴰⵏ, ''Aman Amqran'', "Great Water/Council") is the national [[legislature]] of Tamazgha. The name derives from the Imfezzan word for "water," reflecting the tradition of holding councils at wells and springs—the gathering places essential to desert life.

The Grand Aman is [[W:Bicameralism|bicameral]]:

* '''[[Council of Elders (Tamazgha)|Council of Elders]]''' (''Aman n-Ighallan''): The [[upper house]], composed of hereditary tribal elders, religious scholars, and appointed dignitaries. It reviews legislation for compatibility with customary law and tradition.

* '''[[Assembly of Delegates (Tamazgha)|Assembly of Delegates]]''' (''Aman n-Izimziren''): The [[lower house]], composed of elected representatives from administrative districts. It initiates legislation on domestic matters and approves the national budget.

